venv/
.env
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# Repo-root CLAUDE.md carries local machine paths (real name leak via /Users/<user>/...
# in the "Running things" section) — kept locally, no longer tracked in this public repo.
# Anchored to root only: deck/design/CLAUDE.md is a separate, clean file and stays tracked.
/CLAUDE.md

# Raw Phase 3 survey exports — these contain respondent CONTACT DETAILS (Q18 asked for
# a phone/email for follow-up), and this repo is public. Keep them local only.
# `part2_research_tracker.md` deliberately holds the analysis under anonymised R-numbers
# with "real contact info held separately, not in this doc" — this rule enforces that.
Survey_Responses.pdf
Your Quick-Commerce Shopping Experience*
*Form Responses*
Final_survey.pdf
# Catch-all: any future raw export, whatever it gets named.
*survey*.pdf
*Survey*.pdf
# CSV form exports only. A blanket `*.csv` was too broad — it silently swallowed every
# pipeline export as collateral, so nobody could tell which files were excluded on purpose.
*survey*.csv
*Survey*.csv
*Form Responses*.csv

# Pipeline export of the 1,094 gate-passing extractions. Deliberately NOT committed: it
# carries the full MouthShut review text, which is the one source whose rows exist only in
# the database and in no tracked data/ file. That text embeds reviewer handles
# (e.g. "sky…ocean", "m…") and customer order IDs — pseudonymous identifiers for real
# people. Re-derive it from Postgres instead of publishing it from this public repo.
gate_passing_extractions.csv

# Solution-breakdown report. Kept local only, per explicit instruction — it is an internal
# working document, not a submission deliverable, and it is published as a private Claude
# artifact instead. Do not commit.
docs/solution_breakdown.html

# Interview-framework form (build sheet + Apps Script builder). Kept local only, per explicit
# instruction. These transcribe the PRD brief's own interview questions into a Google Form,
# built after the decision to substitute the N=31 survey for live interviews — publishing them
# in the submission repo would read as backfilling a requirement that was openly scoped out.
# The deviation is declared in part2_research_tracker.md and implementation-plan.md instead.
docs/interview_framework_google_form.md
docs/interview_framework_form_builder.gs

# Playwright MCP scratch output (page snapshots, console logs, screenshots) written into
# the working tree during live QA passes against the deployed Spaces. Transient debug
# artifacts, not project data.
.playwright-mcp/
*.png.tmp
/console-view.png
/hf-01-console.png

# Deck-building working prompts (paste-into-Figma/Design-Labs instructions, revision specs,
# per-slide fix prompts). These are scratch artifacts for iterating on the deck in an external
# tool, not submission content — the deliverable is deck/design/*.dc.html and the exported
# PDF/PPTX. Keep local only.
docs/deck_*.md

# Stitch icon-generation tool exports (zip archives + duplicate code.html previews) used to
# produce a handful of icons now embedded in the deck. Raw tool output, not a deliverable.
deck/design/img/stitch_Design's/
